IMPORT prelude
IMPORT `lss-core`

-- Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) -- THE OWNER'S OR DRIVER'S SEAT: the owner or driver
-- of an uninsured motor vehicle, or another person partly at fault for an injury, from whom the Lifetime Support
-- Authority may recover the cost of an injured participant's care (ss 45, 46). Every question is asked as that person
-- would ask it. The rules are in lss-core.l4; this module restates none of them and defines no name the injured
-- person's seat (lss-seat.l4) defines.
--
-- Based on content from the South Australian Legislation website at 6 November 2026 (version of 2 December 2019).
-- CC BY 4.0. BASELINE ENCODING. Not for public use as advice. See NOTES.md.

§ `The owner's or driver's questions`

§§ `Recovery of the cost of a participant's care (ss 45, 46)`
-- Situation: someone injured in an accident involving you, or a vehicle you own, is a participant in the Lifetime
-- Support Scheme, and the Lifetime Support Authority seeks to recover the cost of their care from you.

@export Can the Lifetime Support Authority recover from me the cost of caring for a person injured in an accident with my uninsured vehicle, or an accident I was partly at fault for, and do I have a defence (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 45)?
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role` @desc Your part in the accident: the owner of the vehicle, with someone else driving; the driver, not the owner; both the owner and the driver; or another person partly at fault who was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle (for example a pedestrian or a road worker)
      `the injured person is a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme
      `they bought in under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person paid the Authority a contribution to buy in to the Scheme under s 6 for those injuries (an accident before 1 July 2014)
      `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in using or operating it
      `the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires (no compulsory third party insurance)
      `the vehicle did not need registration or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, the vehicle was not required to be registered, was exempt from registration, or (if it had to be registered) was not required to be insured under the Motor Vehicles Act 1959
      `I was partly at fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were not an owner or driver: whether the injury was partly the result of your fault
      `I can prove the driver had no authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As owner: whether you can establish to the court's satisfaction that, at the time, someone else was driving the vehicle without your authority
      `I can prove I had authority and believed it was insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As driver: whether you can establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed, and did believe, you had it) and that you reasonably believed, and did believe, the vehicle was insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires
GIVETH A `Recovery answer`
`Can the Authority recover the injured person's care costs from me` MEANS
    `can the Authority recover from this person (s 45)` `my role` `the injured person is a participant` `they bought in under s 6` `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `the vehicle was uninsured` `the vehicle did not need registration or insurance` `I was partly at fault` `I can prove the driver had no authority` `I can prove I had authority and believed it was insured`

@export What is the most the Lifetime Support Authority can recover from me for the cost of caring for an injured participant (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 45(1) to (5))? The answer is in dollars; 0 means s 45 lets it recover nothing from you.
GIVEN `my role` IS A `Role` @desc Your part in the accident: the owner of the vehicle, with someone else driving; the driver, not the owner; both the owner and the driver; or another person partly at fault who was not the owner or driver of a motor vehicle
      `the injured person is a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person is a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme
      `they bought in under s 6` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person paid the Authority a contribution to buy in to the Scheme under s 6 for those injuries
      `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver of a motor vehicle in using or operating it
      `the vehicle was uninsured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time of the accident, the vehicle was not insured as Part 4 of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 requires
      `the vehicle did not need registration or insurance` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether, at the time, the vehicle was not required to be registered, was exempt from registration, or was not required to be insured
      `I was partly at fault` IS A BOOLEAN @desc If you were not an owner or driver: whether the injury was partly the result of your fault
      `I can prove the driver had no authority` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As owner: whether you can establish to the court's satisfaction that someone else was driving without your authority
      `I can prove I had authority and believed it was insured` IS A BOOLEAN @desc As driver: whether you can establish to the court's satisfaction that you drove with the owner's authority (or reasonably believed you had it) and reasonably believed the vehicle was insured
      `the Authority has already paid` IS A NUMBER @desc Dollars the Authority has already paid under Part 4 for the injured person's treatment, care and support needs from the injury
      `the present value of its future payments` IS A NUMBER @desc The present value, in dollars, of what the Authority estimates it will pay in future for those needs (its certificate is evidence of this)
      `the injured person's share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc The injured person's own share in the responsibility for the injury (contributory negligence), as a percentage from 0 to 100
      `my share of responsibility` IS A NUMBER @desc If you were not an owner or driver: your share in the responsibility for the injury, as a percentage from 0 to 100
GIVETH A NUMBER
`What is the most the Authority can recover from me` MEANS
    `the most the Authority can recover (s 45)` (`can the Authority recover from this person (s 45)` `my role` `the injured person is a participant` `they bought in under s 6` `the injury was caused by the fault of the owner or driver` `the vehicle was uninsured` `the vehicle did not need registration or insurance` `I was partly at fault` `I can prove the driver had no authority` `I can prove I had authority and believed it was insured`) `the Authority has already paid` `the present value of its future payments` `the injured person's share of responsibility` `my share of responsibility`

@export My compulsory third party insurer (or the nominal defendant) has a right to recover from me under section 116 or 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959: can the Lifetime Support Authority recover the injured participant's care costs from me in the same way (Motor Vehicle Accidents (Lifetime Support Scheme) Act 2013 (SA) s 46)?
GIVEN `my insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against me` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether an approved insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against you under s 116 or s 124A of the Motor Vehicles Act 1959 for the injury
      `the injured person became a participant` IS A BOOLEAN @desc Whether the injured person became a participant in the Lifetime Support Scheme
GIVETH A `Default recovery answer`
`Can the Authority use my insurer's right of recovery against me` MEANS
    `can the Authority use the right of recovery (s 46)` `my insurer or the nominal defendant has a right of recovery against me` `the injured person became a participant`
